ralph/progress.txt:797:- worker.Loop depends only on the Claimer/Lease interfaces so the durable job store can land later. The loop checks ctx before every Claim (stop claiming on shutdown) and releases interrupted in-flight leases on a context.WithoutCancel context so the release survives shutdown. A job whose Run returns nil is committed and must never be released.
ralph/progress.txt:811:- Quota schema (0006_quota_policy_schema): a closed enum reused across tables is a Postgres DOMAIN over text + CHECK (here quota_resource over 14 dimensions, quota_enforcement_mode over hard/soft/metered/disabled); DROP DOMAIN goes in the down migration after the tables. quota_policies holds one limit per (scope, resource) where a row is EITHER a plan_default (text plan, no plans-table FK yet) OR an organization override — enforced by one table CHECK + two partial unique indexes; the checker resolves "org override else plan default". quota_usage is one counter row per (org, resource); quota_reservations are short-lived (amount>0, status active->committed|released|expired, expires_at, settled_at tied to non-active status by CHECK) and expose UNIQUE (organization_id, id) as a composite-FK target; usage_events is append-only (no updated_at/trigger, signed delta) and links reservations via a tenant-safe composite FK. An optional cross-table link inside a tenant uses a plain composite FK (MATCH SIMPLE) — NOT ON DELETE SET NULL, which would null the NOT NULL organization_id.
ralph/progress.txt:818:- Postgres-backed worker queue (store/job.go ClaimNext, worker/queue.go): the durable queue has two halves. store.JobRepository.ClaimNext is the SKIP LOCKED claim — SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED picks the single most-eligible job (queued|retrying AND next_run_at<=now, OR running AND lease_deadline<now) so concurrent claimers skip a locked row instead of blocking, then transitions it to running inside the same Store.Write tx. An expired-lease job is reclaimed THROUGH the state machine (running->retrying->running, so attempt/lease bookkeeping stays consistent); a job past its retry budget is dead-lettered instead and the poll claims nothing. worker/queue.go is the store-backed Claimer/Lease impl: loop.go stays pure (interfaces only, fake-tested) and queue.go is the only worker file that imports store. Failure classification: worker.Terminal(err)/IsTerminal mark a permanent failure (-> failed, never retried); a plain error is transient (-> retrying with worker.Backoff bounded exponential delay, or -> dead_letter when Attempts>=MaxAttempts). StoreClaimer.complete() records every outcome on a context.WithoutCancel + timeout context — once the runner ran, the outcome write must survive shutdown; only an interrupted (un-run) job returns non-nil from Lease.Run so the loop releases it. The JobRunner (real Dokploy provisioner) is still injected/faked; cmd/yalla-worker stays on NoopClaimer until that runner lands.
