ralph/progress.txt:30544:## 2026-05-18 - BE-0401 - Verification suite: release build tests
ralph/progress.txt:30545:- Implemented the BE-0401 release-build verification gate following the BE-0379..BE-0399 on-every-PR mega-pattern (TWENTY-THIRD worked instance of the verification-suite pattern, NOT opt-in).
ralph/progress.txt:30546:- Created `internal/release/release_build_test.go` with the canonical pair `TestReleaseBuildCoversCallSites` + `TestReleaseBuildPreservesContractUnderContention`. Both members are deterministic — they walk a scenario table built from `release.SupportedTargets` and exercise the pure projection helpers `Target.ArchiveExt`, `Target.BinaryName`, `Target.ArchiveName`, `release.ChecksumsName` with a fixed sample version. The coverage member also pins the exhaustiveness invariant (every documented (OS, arch) coordinate appears exactly once; no off-list coordinate slips in). The contention member fires `releaseBuildWorkers * releaseBuildIterationsPerWorker` = 4096 goroutines against a shared slice and asserts each derives its OWN scenario's predicted projection.
ralph/progress.txt:30547:- Created `internal/release/verification_suite_release_build_static_test.go` pinning SIX surfaces in one file (the standard mega-pattern shape): CI step name + run command, verify.sh required step header `# 25. Required: release build tests` + literal command, CONTRIBUTING.md numbered entry `25. \`go test -run TestReleaseBuild ./...\``, SECURITY.md row + dedicated `## Release Build Tests` section with 14 anchor substrings, PRD `verificationLoop.requiredBackendCommands` entry, and the canonical pair file's existence with both function declarations. Self-check `TestVerificationSuiteReleaseBuildAnalyzerDetectsRegressions` drives every matcher with synthetic known-good AND known-bad fixtures.
ralph/progress.txt:30548:- Inserted `# 25. Required: release build tests` step in `scripts/verify.sh` between BE-0399's #24 and the trailing optionals; renumbered verify.sh optional steps #25-#29 → #26-#30. Updated BE-0400's static test (`verification_suite_external_dokploy_smoke_static_test.go`) header constant from `# 29. Optional…` to `# 30. Optional…` and the synthetic fixtures inside the analyser self-check in the same edit — the renumber is the shared cost of inserting a required step into the sequence and is forward-applicable to every future required-step insertion.
ralph/progress.txt:30552:- Added BE-0401 subsection to `internal/release/AGENTS.md` explaining the static-test contract, the renumber-as-shared-cost convention, and the load-bearing constants.
ralph/progress.txt:30557:- internal/release/release_build_test.go (NEW)
ralph/progress.txt:30558:- internal/release/verification_suite_release_build_static_test.go (NEW)
ralph/progress.txt:30559:- internal/release/verification_suite_external_dokploy_smoke_static_test.go (MODIFIED — renumber #29 → #30 + synthetic-fixture #28 → #29)
ralph/progress.txt:30560:- internal/release/AGENTS.md (MODIFIED — appended BE-0401 subsection)
ralph/progress.txt:30570:- `go test ./internal/release/...` → 0.305s ok (canonical pair + static gate + analyser self-check + existing release_test.go all pass)
ralph/progress.txt:30572:- `go test -race ./...` → all packages ok, exit 0; release package took 2.020s under -race with the 4096-goroutine burst — clean
ralph/progress.txt:30578:- **Inserting a required verify.sh step at position #N forces a renumber of every optional step #N..end AND a synchronised constant update in every prior static test that pinned an affected step header.** For BE-0401, that meant updating BE-0400's external-smoke static test (`externalDokploySmokeVerifyShStepHeader` from `# 29` to `# 30`; the synthetic-fixture strings inside the analyser self-check from `# 28`/`# 29` to `# 29`/`# 30`) in the same edit. The renumber cost is bounded: only static tests that pin step headers in the affected range need updates, and the existing matchers fail loudly on drift so the renumber lands deterministically. Forward-applicable to every future required-step insertion: grep all `# N. Optional` and `# N. Required` literals in `internal/release/verification_suite_*_static_test.go` for the renumbered range and update each in the same commit.
ralph/progress.txt:30579:- **Pure projection helpers (no live infrastructure) still benefit from a contention-burst member of the canonical pair.** The release package's `ArchiveExt`/`BinaryName`/`ArchiveName`/`ChecksumsName` are pure functions today, so the contention member would seem redundant. But the burst is the load-bearing stability check the gate's wire contract requires: a future regression that introduced shared mutable state (a cached lookup table, a global builder, a sync.Once that mutated a shared map) would surface here before reaching the GoReleaser pipeline. Keeping the pair shape consistent across every BE-0379..BE-0401 verification gate makes the static analyser's canonical-funcs matcher reusable and the operator-facing AGENTS.md narrative consistent. Forward-applicable: every future verification-suite gate (pure-function or stateful) keeps the closed-set-coverage + per-decision-stability pair shape so the `-run TestX` filter binds to a two-function fixture the static gate can name.
ralph/progress.txt:30580:- **The static gate's SECURITY.md substring matcher tolerates 14 anchor substrings without the inline pattern feeling brittle.** Using semantically anchored substrings (function names, type names, file names, contract keywords) instead of whole sentences keeps the matcher robust to Markdown line wrap while still pinning every AC. The choice to exclude `policy.Engine`-style backtick-quoted code spans from the substring set when they don't apply to the gate (release-build has no policy boundary) keeps the matcher focused on the load-bearing facts.
ralph/progress.txt:30586:- Created `internal/release/verification_suite_config_validation_static_test.go` pinning SIX surfaces in one file (the standard mega-pattern shape): CI step name + run command, verify.sh required step header `# 26. Required: config validation tests` + literal command, CONTRIBUTING.md numbered entry `26. \`go test -run TestConfigValidation ./...\``, SECURITY.md row + dedicated `## Config Validation Tests` section with 14 anchor substrings (internal/controlplane/config, config_validation_test.go, deterministic, CodeConfig, strict-profile, YALLA_DATABASE_URL, YALLA_SECRET_KEYS, MapLookup, yalla.error.v1, the two function names, Every push and PR, redact, and the self-locating static-test filename), PRD `verificationLoop.requiredBackendCommands` entry, and the canonical pair file's existence with both function declarations. Self-check `TestVerificationSuiteConfigValidationAnalyzerDetectsRegressions` drives every matcher with synthetic known-good AND known-bad fixtures.
ralph/progress.txt:30587:- Inserted `# 26. Required: config validation tests` step in `scripts/verify.sh` between BE-0401's #25 and the trailing optionals (renumbered #26-#30 → #27-#31 in the same edit). Updated BE-0400's static test (`externalDokploySmokeVerifyShStepHeader` from `# 30` to `# 31`; the synthetic-fixture strings inside the analyser self-check from `# 29`/`# 30` to `# 30`/`# 31`) and the prose comment that documented the trailing-optional position (`#30` → `#31` + the `#26..#29 govulncheck..goreleaser` enumeration shifted to `#27..#30`).
