ralph/progress.txt:34195:  - The idempotency_keys CHECK constraint `idempotency_keys_completion_consistent` is the load-bearing reason the byte-identity comparator MUST switch on nil-ness FIRST and dereference value SECOND. A naive field-equality loop would silently round-trip a regression that flipped a pending row's NULL completion columns to zero-value scalars (response_status=0, response_body=[]byte{}, completed_at=epoch) — the schema would reject this on INSERT but the test would not catch it on a peer-row drift. Forward-applicable to any future tenant-isolation file whose row carries nullable completion columns: job_attempts (nullable error_summary / finished_at / result), quota_reservations (nullable released_at / job_id), break_glass_sessions (nullable revoked_at).
